      "title": "H3 edit prompt | <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.45.0",
        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ImageConditioning"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edit <Picture 1>. Replace the facial identity of the main person with the facial identity from <Picture 2>.\n\n<Picture 1> defines the original photograph, including the scene, camera perspective, head orientation, hairstyle, accessories, clothing, body, lighting, and background.\n\n<Picture 2> provides the facial identity of the replacement person, including eye shape and spacing, nose, lips, cheekbones, jawline, facial proportions, skin characteristics, and distinctive facial details.\n\nTransfer the facial identity from <Picture 2> with maximum accuracy and fidelity, preserving the recognizable features and unique characteristics of the reference person.\n\nCreate one natural, believable photograph in which the person from <Picture 2> appears in the scene from <Picture 1>.\n\nAdapt the transferred face naturally to the original head orientation, expression, perspective, and lighting.\n\nAllow subtle adjustments to the surrounding facial contours, hairline, nearby hair strands, shadows, and skin transitions wherever necessary to achieve a seamless and anatomically coherent result.\n\nPreserve the overall hairstyle, hair color, hair length, and appearance from <Picture 1>, but allow minor natural adjustments to accommodate the replacement face.\n\nHair from <Picture 2> must not be transferred as part of the facial identity. Any bangs, fringe, or hair covering the reference face should be treated as separate from the facial features.\n\nAvoid overlapping hairstyles, duplicated hair, ghosting, unnatural facial boundaries, or a pasted-on appearance.\n\nPreserve the original accessories, clothing, body, background, and overall composition.\n\nPrioritize accurate facial identity and natural visual integration over rigid pixel-level preservation.\n\nThe final result must look like a genuine photograph, not a digitally pasted face.",
        2048,
        2048
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "prompt": "Edit <Picture 1>. Replace the facial identity of the main person with the facial identity from <Picture 2>.\n\n<Picture 1> defines the original photograph, including the scene, camera perspective, head orientation, hairstyle, accessories, clothing, body, lighting, and background.\n\n<Picture 2> provides the facial identity of the replacement person, including eye shape and spacing, nose, lips, cheekbones, jawline, facial proportions, skin characteristics, and distinctive facial details.\n\nTransfer the facial identity from <Picture 2> with maximum accuracy and fidelity, preserving the recognizable features and unique characteristics of the reference person.\n\nCreate one natural, believable photograph in which the person from <Picture 2> appears in the scene from <Picture 1>.\n\nAdapt the transferred face naturally to the original head orientation, expression, perspective, and lighting.\n\nAllow subtle adjustments to the surrounding facial contours, hairline, nearby hair strands, shadows, and skin transitions wherever necessary to achieve a seamless and anatomically coherent result.\n\nPreserve the overall hairstyle, hair color, hair length, and appearance from <Picture 1>, but allow minor natural adjustments to accommodate the replacement face.\n\nHair from <Picture 2> must not be transferred as part of the facial identity. Any bangs, fringe, or hair covering the reference face should be treated as separate from the facial features.\n\nAvoid overlapping hairstyles, duplicated hair, ghosting, unnatural facial boundaries, or a pasted-on appearance.\n\nPreserve the original accessories, clothing, body, background, and overall composition.\n\nPrioritize accurate facial identity and natural visual integration over rigid pixel-level preservation.\n\nThe final result must look like a genuine photograph, not a digitally pasted face.",
        "width": 2048,
        "height": 2048
      }
    },
